Found under k275 (2026-10-31, ocp-status-worker). `OCP::K8s->register` writes OCPNode/OCPNodeProvider into `$api->resource_map`; `invalidate_discovery` drops what it wrote, and `ensure_crd` calls `invalidate_discovery`. So the apply API and the other ~15 `register` callers lose OCPNode and OCPNodeProvider after an `ensure_crd` in the same process, and a later `list/get(OCPNode)` dies "unknown resource" before any request.

k275 fixed `OCP::Kubernetes` (ocp status) by pushing the two kinds onto `$api->with` instead, which is read lazily and survives rebuilds; robocop's Controller still calls `register` on top.

Done = reproduce (a test: register → ensure_crd → list OCPNode), then fix in one place — likely `OCP::K8s->register` itself using the `with` list — so every caller keeps the kinds across a discovery rebuild; check whether any apply path already hit this live.

